# Integer128 literal above the maximum

Binds 170141183460469231731687303715884105728, one past the 128-bit
maximum, to verify the literal is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic
instead of wrapping.

>>> source
too_large: int128 = 170141183460469231731687303715884105728
print(too_large)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `170141183460469231731687303715884105728` for type `int128`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 20, end: 59 }

<<< exit
1
